      "mergeID": "5be914f14fc3a71d4d4b38a3",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I use the samsung Odyssey headset and I have no issue at all playing the game. I was wondering though since the mixed reality controllers have both touchpad and thumb stick, I would love if there was a way to use the thumbsticks for movement, and the touch pads for only the gestures. I always activate gestures while moving around so it would be awesome if I could separate the controls.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Windows MR controller",
      "parentID": "5acb81c455478a54b4889930",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "59c7ca118aa3b20425cab781",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "@{5a7052a4337de65dbe2d96b2|full_name}: EDIT: sorry I was wrong and stumbled across it.\n\nTo enable it, per this thread on reddit:\nhttps://www.reddit.com/r/WindowsMR/comments/7un535/wmr_thumbstick_turning_in_steamvr_is_awesome_is/du7q93w\n\n\"Go to (your steamlibrary folder)\\steamapps\\common\\MixedRealityVRDriver\\resources\\settings\nThen in default.vrsettings replace false with true next to thumbstickControlsEnabled!\"",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
